  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "If Problem 17.64 has an affirmative answer, does it follow that, for some\nfunction g(p), the number of isomorphism classes of g(p)-approximations to J is\n   a) countable?\n   b) one?\nNote that if, for some g(p), there are only finitely many isomorphism classes, then for\nsome h(p) there is only one.                                     C. R. Leedham-Green",
